From 4687007e00849b555ac23934ddefb3445f8f2c2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mei Tao <gonzolesopela896@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:39:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH v1 2/2] libcamera: software_isp: Apply LSC gains to the
 statistics on the GPU path

The software ISP gathers AWB sums and an AGC luminance histogram from raw
Bayer samples, while the GPU applies lens shading correction separately.
Dark corners therefore lower the measured brightness and can make AGC
increase exposure even when the corrected image is already bright.
Colour-dependent shading also biases grey-world AWB, which should use
means corrected for the same shading as the rendered image.

Pass the per-frame LSC state with the debayer parameters and apply the
current table to sampled Bayer components before accumulating statistics.
Cache four Q10 gains per sampled cell, including separate green gains,
and rebuild the map only when the table version or window changes. Keep
the black pedestal so the existing AWB and AGC black subtraction remains
valid. The statistics stay before AWB gains and the colour matrix.

Match the shader's bilinear, clamp-to-edge RGBA8 field and byte * 4 / 255
scale, including texel-centre coordinates and input stride. Q10 rounding
limits the gain error to 1/2048. Preserve the existing sparse sampling and
leave statistics unchanged when LSC is disabled. The CPU renderer does not
apply LSC, so it passes the frame parameters with LSC unavailable and
retains raw statistics.

On a Lenovo ThinkSmart View with S5KC505A and qcom-camss, a neutral surface
was about 5% warm before the correction. Reported measurements with the
corrected statistics are R/G = 0.999 and B/G = 0.983. The AGC luminance
target previously had to be reduced to 0.10 to avoid over-exposure; 0.12
can now be used, closer to the default 0.16. Grey-world scene-colour bias
and differences from full demosaiced output statistics remain.
Cross-compilation and standalone QEMU tests cover the existing Bayer
formats, phase and window mapping, black-level handling, saturation,
histograms, cache invalidation and enabled/disabled transitions.

Signed-off-by: Mei Tao <gonzolesopela896@gmail.com>
